From the KISA guide (주요정보통신기반시설 기술적 취약점 분석·평가 방법 상세가이드) this
repository reproduces only item codes, item names, categories, importance levels
and page numbers, as a cross-reference index. Control titles, descriptions and
rationale are muster's own wording; no inspection, criterion or remediation text
from the guide is included, and the guide itself is not included.

CIS Benchmark references are benchmark name, version and recommendation number
only. No CIS Benchmark text is included and no CIS compliance level is claimed.
See ATTRIBUTION.md.

The `cis-<distro>-l1` profiles select muster's own controls that carry a CIS
Benchmark recommendation number at Level 1 – Server; their results are
muster's verdicts on muster's controls, not a CIS assessment, and muster is an
independent publication not authorized, sponsored or otherwise approved by the
Center for Internet Security.

DISA STIG and CCI identifiers are drawn from works of the United States
Government, not subject to copyright in the United States (17 U.S.C. § 105).
This repository reproduces only STIG and CCI identifiers, severities and
titles, never their discussion, check and fix text. See ATTRIBUTION.md.

ComplianceAsCode

The CIS recommendation numbers and levels in docs/reference/cis/, the
ComplianceAsCode rule ids in docs/reference/cis/map.yaml and the cis-*-l1
profiles generated from them (embedded in the binary) are derived from
ComplianceAsCode/content (https://github.com/ComplianceAsCode/content), tag
v0.1.82, commit 3da954fbccfb4ca611da86c9be9205d83c38bfc7, files
controls/cis_ubuntu2204.yml, controls/cis_ubuntu2404.yml,
products/rhel9/controls/cis_rhel9.yml and controls/cis_almalinux9.yml.
From each pinned file `tools/cisindex` decodes exactly the header's `version`
and each entry's `id`, `levels` and `rules`; `title`, `notes`, `status`,
`related_rules` and every other field never leave its decoder, and no
Benchmark text is stored.
